                <pb facs="0293" n="205" sameAs="frus:frus1933v04/pg205"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">810.7962/2: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to the Chairman of the American Delegation</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Hull</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1933-12-23T10:00:00-05:00">December 23, 1933—10
                        a.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>117. Department’s 101, December 19, 7 p.m. The President hopes that progress can
                    be made with respect to fast air communication and establishment beacons and
                    guides before adjournment of conference. He suggests that a conference of
                    experts of the interested countries to be held in Washington might be
                    helpful.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Phillips</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
